{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Licensee is identified only as \"you\", with no named person or entity in the operative granting sentence, so who is bound (Garrett Salpeter personally or ARPwave Austin LLC, his employer on the form above) is genuinely open. \"the ARP POV System, described above\" also points to a form that describes only quantity and price, not a system.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.62},
     {"issue": "The heading and grant call this a \"BRONZE SYSTEM LICENSE\" of \"the ARP POV System\", while section 1.1 defines System(s) as all intellectual property and equipment associated with ARP Wave LLC and section 1.2 limits the license to five enumerated items; the three descriptions of the licensed subject matter do not line up.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"all other intellectual property and equipment associated with ARP Wave LLC\" has no discernible boundary — \"associated with\" could reach every protocol, program and device the Licensor owns — and the enumerated \"proprietary protocols and programs\" sit against that open-ended catch-all. \"Used commercially\" is likewise undefined for a licensee whose stated business is operating an ARPwave clinic.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.58},
     {"issue": "\"This agreement is non-cancellable for any reason\" cannot be squared with section 7.1 (revocation \"if this Agreement is terminated\"), 7.2 (\"Upon termination of this Agreement for any reason\") and 7.3 (survival after termination), all of which presuppose that the Agreement can be terminated.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.55}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The license is granted for the ARP POV SYSTEM \"which consists of the following\" five items, an exhaustive enumeration inviting an expressio unius reading, yet items such as \"DISCOUNTS ON CUSTOM TRAINING PROGRAMS AND PROTOCOLS\" state no discount and no term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": "The closed five-item list conflicts with the far broader definition of \"System(s)\" in section 1.1 (all protocols, programs, intellectual property and equipment associated with ARP Wave LLC), leaving it unclear which body of material the licence, confidentiality (3.2) and return (7.2) obligations attach to.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.42}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The clause sets a 60-month \"original term\" but then lets the Licensee keep the System(s) indefinitely afterwards \"at no additional charge\" except for unspecified \"charges applicable for time use\" at rates \"set forth on page one\", which the attached form does not set out.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
     {"issue": "A definite 60-month term with a \"License End Date\" is hard to reconcile with section 1.1's statement that the agreement \"is non-cancellable for any reason\" and with sections 7.1-7.3, which contemplate termination and post-termination return of the System(s).", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The rights are said to be \"forfeitable in the event of certain circumstances or occurrences as herein set forth\", but the phrase names no circumstance and points nowhere identifiable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
     {"issue": "The cross-reference to forfeiture events \"as herein set forth\" has no referent: Section 5 (Default) never defines an event of default, and no other provision enumerates forfeiture triggers.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.09},
     {"issue": "Section 1.5 bars enhancements without consent, while section 7.2 requires return of \"enhancements\" on termination, implying they may exist; the tension is minor and readily harmonised.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Misuse or negligence on the part of Licensee\" is the sole allocator of repair cost and is left wholly undefined, and \"defects\" is not distinguished from ordinary wear.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
     {"issue": "Free repair is promised only \"during the original term\", which sits awkwardly with section 1.3's provision that the Licensee may keep the unit indefinitely after the original term at no additional charge.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.17}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
     {"issue": "The duty to \"keep the ARP POV Unit in good repair\" overlaps with section 2.1's promise of free Licensor repair during the original term, but the two are reconcilable through the misuse/negligence carve-out.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Full replacement value thereof as determined by the Licensor\" leaves the insured amount to one party's unilateral determination while also fixing it at $7560.00, and the required \"liability and property damage insurance\" has no stated limit.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
     {"issue": "The stated replacement value of $7560.00 does not match the \"Total Cost Of Plans: $7500\" recorded on the face of the same instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"The Protocols licensed in conjunction with the System(s)\" is capitalised as if defined but is never defined, and \"acting outside the scope of use\" gives no ascertainable boundary for the conduct required.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The confidentiality duty attaches to \"all System(s)\", which under section 1.1 includes physical equipment, and there is no carve-out for information already public or independently known, so the reach of the secrecy obligation is genuinely uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
     {"issue": "A duty to keep the System(s) \"strictly confidential\" and not to \"display\" them is hard to reconcile with the licensed use contemplated by section 1.2 (applying the unit to an \"applicatee\" under section 3.1), and with section 1.3's continuing possession right.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The disclaimer excludes \"warranties of marketability\" rather than merchantability, a mechanical error that may defeat the disclaimer of the implied warranty of merchantability, which by statute must be mentioned by name.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.37},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The first sentence preserves claims for \"breach or breaches of Licensor's contractual obligations herein set forth\" while the second waives \"all rights at law and equity\" to claim fraud, imperfection or \"any form of redress with respect to said System(s)\", so the scope of what survives the waiver is internally uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.47},
     {"issue": "The blanket waiver of fraud claims sits against section 5.2 and Section 4's other disclaimers, and against the Licensor's affirmative repair obligation in section 2.1, which the waiver would render unenforceable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]}
]}

